       e.title, e.snippet, e.content_json, e.status, $s$Restored from the snapshot taken before the lecture-notes removal$s$, null
  FROM public.essays e WHERE e.id = 'd035aea1-7784-4c3c-9da1-d942b016fedc';

-- long-term-investments-splitting-a-fall
UPDATE public.essays
   SET content = $c$<p><strong>In brief</strong></p><ul><li><p>The line mixes holdings under different rules. Associates (significant influence) and joint ventures (joint control of net assets) use the equity method, small equity stakes sit at fair value, and some debt sits at amortised cost. Subsidiaries never appear on the consolidated line.</p></li><li><p>An equity-method investment falls with every dividend received, because the profit behind the dividend was booked when the investee earned it. A profitable associate that pays out generously shrinks the line.</p></li><li><p>A fall has five possible sources (shares of losses, dividends, impairment, disposal or reclassification, and fair-value or currency changes), and only some are losses. In the constructed 2025 case, USD 29.0 million of a USD 49.0 million fall is cash received or a move to current assets.</p></li></ul><hr><h2>The line fell 30.8 percent, and the page alone cannot say how much of that was a loss</h2><p>On the page, long-term investments fell from 1,602,821 at 31 December 2023 to 1,109,172 at 31 December 2024, in thousands, a fall of 493,649 or 30.8 percent. The line's share of total assets dropped from 5.1 percent to 3.7 percent, and the page gives no notes reference for it.</p><p>PT Hulu Energi Nusantara ("HEN") is an upstream contractor operating production sharing contracts (PSCs) with SKK Migas, the government body that supervises upstream oil and gas. HEN is fictional and every HEN figure is constructed. It reports in US dollars under Indonesian SAK, and all HEN amounts are in USD million. At the audit committee meeting on the 2025 accounts, a member reads that long-term investments fell from USD 160.0 million at 31 December 2024 to USD 111.0 million at 31 December 2025, a fall of 30.6 percent, and asks two questions. Did HEN lose USD 49.0 million on its stakes? And should the committee accept management's USD 17.0 million write-down of HEN's LNG joint venture?</p><p>The governing claim of this essay is that a fall in long-term investments says nothing about value until it is split by mechanism. Dividends from equity-method investees and reclassifications to current assets reduce the line without any loss, while shares of profit and loss, impairments and fair-value changes record changes in value, and each follows its own rule. This is a mechanism essay. Its verdict is that USD 29.0 million of HEN's fall is cash received or a change of line, and USD 20.0 million is a net value change (USD 32.0 million of losses against USD 12.0 million of share of profit). The figure the committee must challenge is the USD 17.0 million impairment, because it rests on management's own forecast.</p><p>PSAK numbers follow the 2024 scheme (old numbers: 228 was 15, 109 was 71, 236 was 48, 111 was 66, 110 was 65, 201 was 1, 221 was 10); IFRS equivalents are in the references.</p><h2>The line holds whatever the investor influences without controlling, and subsidiaries never sit on it</h2><p>Which rule measures a holding depends on the investor's power over the investee, and the ownership percentage only guides that judgment. HEN's line held five items:</p><table style="min-width: 125px;"><colgroup><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Holding</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Stake</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Relationship</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Measurement</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>31 Dec 2024, USD million</p></th></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>PT Pipa Gas Selat, gas pipeline</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>30%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Associate</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Equity method</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>62.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>PT Kilang LNG Timur, LNG plant</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>50%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Joint venture</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Equity method</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>48.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>PT Cakra Eksplorasi, holds an exploration PSC</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>25%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Associate</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Equity method</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>6.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>PT Jasa Sumur Tbk (listed), oilfield services</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>4%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Equity instrument</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Fair value through other comprehensive income, elected</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>30.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Republic of Indonesia USD bond, due 30 June 2026</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>n/a</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Debt instrument</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Amortised cost</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>14.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p><strong>Total</strong></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p><strong>160.0</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Below 20 percent an equity investor is presumed to lack significant influence, and PSAK 109 measures the shares at fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL), unless the investor elects at initial recognition, irrevocably and for shares not held for trading, to send fair-value changes to other comprehensive income (FVOCI). From 20 to 50 percent the investor is presumed to have significant influence, the power to take part in the investee's financial and operating decisions without controlling them, and PSAK 228 requires the equity method. Both presumptions can be rebutted. A joint venture, where the parties share control by unanimous consent and have rights to the net assets, also uses the equity method. Control under PSAK 110, usually but not always gained through a majority of the votes, replaces the investment with the subsidiary's assets and liabilities line by line. The study notes show a subsidiary as a long-term investment, which holds only in the parent's separate statements.</p><p>Debt is sorted by two tests in PSAK 109, the business model (hold to collect, collect and sell, or neither) and whether the contractual cash flows are only principal and interest on the principal. HEN holds its 5 percent bond, bought at par, to maturity, so it sits at amortised cost. A bond held to collect and sell would sit at FVOCI and recycle on sale, meaning the gains parked in OCI are moved into profit when the bond is sold.</p><p>The notes impair amortised-cost debt only after a loss event; PSAK 109 replaced that incurred-loss approach with expected credit losses (ECL), booked from the day of purchase. Stage 1 carries twelve months of expected loss. Stage 2 carries lifetime loss once credit risk has risen significantly. Stage 3, once the borrower has actually defaulted or is in severe distress (credit-impaired), keeps lifetime loss but computes interest income on the carrying amount net of the allowance. HEN's bond is in stage 1, where the allowance multiplies the chance of default within a year, the share lost on default, and the amount at risk:</p><blockquote><p><strong>12-month ECL = probability of default × loss given default × exposure</strong></p><p><strong>= 0.3% × 40% × USD 14.0 million = USD 0.0168 million</strong></p></blockquote><p>The allowance rounds to zero at one decimal, so the bond is carried at USD 14.0 million. It also marks the line's current boundary. At 31 December 2025 it falls due within twelve months, so PSAK 201 moves USD 14.0 million to current assets with no change in value. An equity-method investment stays non-current unless it is held for sale under PSAK 105 (was 58).</p><h2>Under the equity method a dividend is cash leaving the investment, because the profit behind it was booked when the investee earned it</h2><p>The equity method treats the stake as a claim on the investee's net assets, booking income when they grow and cash, but no income, when they are paid out. HEN bought 30 percent of PT Pipa Gas Selat on 1 January 2023 for USD 56.0 million, exactly 30 percent of its fair net assets, so no goodwill sits inside the investment:</p><table style="min-width: 100px;"><colgroup><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>USD million</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>2023</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>2024</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>2025</p></th></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Opening carrying amount</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>56.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>59.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>62.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Pipeline net profit, 100%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>30.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>36.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>40.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Add HEN's 30% share of profit</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>9.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>10.8</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>12.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Pipeline dividends paid, 100%</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>20.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>26.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>50.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Less HEN's 30% of dividends</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>6.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>7.8</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>15.0</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Closing carrying amount</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>59.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>62.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>59.0</p></td></tr></tbody></table><blockquote><p><strong>Dr Investment in associate 12.0 / Cr Share of profit of associates 12.0</strong></p><p><strong>Dr Cash 15.0 / Cr Investment in associate 15.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>The pipeline's USD 40.0 million profit raised HEN's claim by USD 12.0 million, recognised as income. Its USD 50.0 million dividend cut the claim by USD 15.0 million and raised HEN's cash by the same amount. Booking the 15.0 as income too would report 27.0 of income on 12.0 of earnings and leave 74.0 on the line while 15.0 sat in the bank. The pipeline used cash released by refinancing its own debt to pay out 125 percent of its 2025 profit, so HEN's most profitable associate shrank the line by USD 3.0 million in its best year.</p><h2>An equity-method investment is tested for impairment as one asset, so the whole write-down can later be reversed</h2><p>PT Kilang LNG Timur's commissioning, the testing and start-up of the plant, slipped by a year in 2025, and its buyers reopened the offtake price, the contracted price for the LNG they take. The joint venture lost USD 8.0 million in the year, of which HEN's half is USD 4.0 million:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Dr Share of loss of joint ventures 4.0 / Cr Investment in joint venture 4.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>Evidence such as a significant adverse change in the investee's market (IAS 28 paragraphs 41A–41C) triggers a test of the whole carrying amount under PSAK 236. The carrying amount is compared with the recoverable amount, the higher of value in use (the present value of the cash flows the investment is expected to produce) and fair value less costs of disposal. Management's discounted model of HEN's share of the joint venture's cash flows gives a value in use of USD 27.0 million (constructed input). A buyer has offered USD 25.0 million, non-binding, and selling would cost USD 0.5 million.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Carrying amount before the test = 48.0 − 4.0 = 44.0</strong></p><p><strong>Fair value less costs of disposal = 25.0 − 0.5 = 24.5</strong></p><p><strong>Recoverable amount = higher of 27.0 and 24.5 = 27.0</strong></p><p><strong>Impairment loss = 44.0 − 27.0 = 17.0</strong></p><p><strong>Dr Impairment loss on investment in joint venture 17.0 / Cr Investment in joint venture 17.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>The loss is larger than HEN's whole 12.0 share of the pipeline's profit in its best year.</p><p>PSAK 236 never reverses a goodwill impairment, so it matters that an equity-method investment is tested as one asset and no part of its loss is allocated to goodwill inside it (IAS 28 paragraph 42). HEN paid no premium for Kilang either. If the estimates behind the recoverable amount improve, for example once the plant starts up, all USD 17.0 million can be reversed, up to the carrying amount the investment would have had without the impairment.</p><p>Every USD 1.0 million added to value in use removes USD 1.0 million of loss until value in use reaches USD 44.0 million; on the downside the fair-value floor of USD 24.5 million caps the loss at USD 19.5 million.</p><h2>When the share of losses exceeds the investment, the investor stops at zero and tracks the rest off the books</h2><p>PT Cakra Eksplorasi drilled a dry exploration well in 2025, wrote off its exploration and evaluation assets under PSAK 106 (was 64), and reported a net loss after tax of USD 40.0 million (constructed). HEN's 25 percent share is larger than its investment:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Share of loss = 25% × 40.0 = 10.0</strong></p><p><strong>Loss recognised, limited to the carrying amount = 6.0</strong></p><p><strong>Loss not recognised, tracked outside the accounts = 10.0 − 6.0 = 4.0</strong></p><p><strong>Dr Share of loss of associates 6.0 / Cr Investment in associate 6.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>PSAK 228 stops loss recognition when the investor's interest reaches zero (IAS 28 paragraphs 38–39). The interest includes long-term interests that form part of the net investment, such as a shareholder loan with no planned repayment. Beyond them a liability arises only from a legal obligation, a constructive obligation (one created by the investor's own conduct or promises), or payments made on the associate's behalf. HEN has none of these. If Cakra earns USD 20.0 million in 2026, HEN's share is USD 5.0 million, the first USD 4.0 million offsets the unrecognised loss, and HEN books USD 1.0 million.</p><p>A commitment to meet an associate's cash calls (the operator's requests for each partner's share of spending) may be the obligation that turns an unrecognised loss into a provision.</p><h2>Below 20 percent at FVOCI, the dividend is income and the value change never reaches profit</h2><p>HEN holds 200 million shares of PT Jasa Sumur Tbk, 4 percent of the company, to secure drilling services, and elected FVOCI when it bought them. The shares trade in rupiah. Under PSAK 221 their fair value is translated at the rate on the measurement date, and because an FVOCI share's whole fair-value change goes to OCI, the currency part goes there too.</p><blockquote><p><strong>31 Dec 2024: 200 million × IDR 2,400 = IDR 480 billion; at IDR 16,000 per USD = USD 30.0 million</strong></p><p><strong>31 Dec 2025: 200 million × IDR 2,080 = IDR 416 billion; at IDR 16,640 per USD = USD 25.0 million</strong></p><p><strong>Price effect, at the opening rate = 200 million × (IDR 2,080 − IDR 2,400) / 16,000 = −USD 4.0 million</strong></p><p><strong>Currency effect = IDR 416 billion / 16,640 − IDR 416 billion / 16,000 = 25.0 − 26.0 = −USD 1.0 million</strong></p><p><strong>Dr Other comprehensive income, fair value reserve 5.0 / Cr Investment in equity instruments 5.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>Both effects land in the same reserve; the reader's split shows that one fifth of the fall comes from the dollar strengthening 4 percent against the rupiah, from IDR 16,000 to IDR 16,640.</p><p>Jasa Sumur also paid a dividend of IDR 80 a share, IDR 16 billion in total, received when the rate was IDR 16,000:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Dr Cash 1.0 / Cr Dividend income 1.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>Here the dividend is income, because HEN never booked a share of Jasa Sumur's profit; the exception is a dividend that clearly recovers part of the cost. The fair-value loss never reaches profit. FVOCI equity has no impairment test under PSAK 109, and on sale the cumulative reserve may move to retained earnings within equity but is never recycled (IFRS 9 paragraphs 5.7.5 and B5.7.1). The USD 5.0 million fall reduces HEN's total comprehensive income and leaves its profit untouched in every year.</p><h2>A participating interest in a PSC is usually a joint operation, so most of an upstream group's partnerships never reach this line</h2><p>An upstream group's most common partnership, a participating interest in a PSC shared under a joint operating agreement, usually stays off this line. Under PSAK 111, parties to a joint operation have rights to the assets and obligations for the liabilities and recognise their own shares of each, while parties to a joint venture have rights only to the net assets and use the equity method. A contractor party to the PSC takes its share of production and bears its share of costs, the profile of a joint operation. Many operating agreements let a majority of partners decide, so no joint control exists and the arrangement falls outside PSAK 111, but each partner still recognises its own share. Either way, a participating interest held directly by HEN would appear inside oil and gas properties, receivables, payables, revenue and costs.</p><p>The boundary moves with the legal vehicle. Indonesian practice ring-fences PSCs, keeping each contract's costs and taxes separate and often holding each contract in its own company, so a partner may own shares in that company instead of the participating interest. HEN's 25 percent of PT Cakra Eksplorasi is that case, an associate measured in one line although its economics resemble a 25 percent participating interest. A separate company points toward a joint venture without settling it, because the agreements decide: if they give the parties the output and make them fund the liabilities, PSAK 111 still finds a joint operation.</p><h2>HEN's USD 49.0 million fall is USD 29.0 million of cash and reclassification and a USD 20.0 million net value change</h2><p>Only one row of HEN's 2025 roll-forward rests on HEN management's own forecast. The rest come from the investees' audited results, a quoted price, an exchange rate or a maturity date.</p><table style="min-width: 100px;"><colgroup><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"><col style="min-width: 25px;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Mechanism</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Holding</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>USD million</p></th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Nature</p></th></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>31 Dec 2024</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>160.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Share of profit</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Pipa Gas Selat</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>+12.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Share of loss</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Kilang LNG Timur</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−4.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Share of loss, limited to carrying amount</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Cakra Eksplorasi</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−6.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Dividends received</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Pipa Gas Selat</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−15.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Cash</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Impairment</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Kilang LNG Timur</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−17.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Fair value, price</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Jasa Sumur</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−4.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Fair value, currency</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Jasa Sumur</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−1.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Value</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Reclassified to current assets</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Bond</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>−14.0</p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p>Line</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p><strong>31 Dec 2025</strong></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p><strong>111.0</strong></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p></p></td></tr></tbody></table><blockquote><p><strong>Change = 111.0 − 160.0 = −49.0, or −30.6%</strong></p><p><strong>Cash received and change of line = 15.0 + 14.0 = 29.0</strong></p><p><strong>Losses = 4.0 + 6.0 + 17.0 + 4.0 + 1.0 = 32.0</strong></p><p><strong>Net value change recognised in profit and OCI = 32.0 − 12.0 = 20.0</strong></p></blockquote><p>Profit for 2025 carries 12.0 − 4.0 − 6.0 − 17.0 = −15.0 of the net value change and OCI −5.0. Pairing the pipeline's profit with value and its dividend with cash is a choice of presentation; netting the two instead would show only 3.0 of dividends in excess of earnings.</p><p>HEN did not lose USD 49.0 million. It recognised USD 32.0 million of losses against USD 12.0 million of share of profit, and USD 17.0 million of those losses rests on a forecast. The committee should not accept the impairment until management has tested the three inputs that drive value in use (the commissioning date, the renegotiated offtake price and the discount rate), and should require disclosure under PSAK 112 of the USD 4.0 million unrecognised loss in Cakra with any funding commitment behind it.</p><p>A reader of the reported page can triangulate from the share of results and impairment lines in the income statement, dividends received in the cash flow statement, and fair-value movements in OCI. No current line that could hold a reclassified investment grew materially (other current assets rose 1,997 thousand), and the page has no short-term investment or held-for-sale line, so it shows no sign of a large reclassification.</p><h3>Least-confident assertions</h3><ul><li><p>The joint operation reading of a PSC participating interest is the usual pattern, not a verified rule. Whether joint control exists depends on the operating agreement's voting terms, and where a PSC is held through a ring-fenced company the classification under PSAK 111 turns on that company's agreements. No actual PSC or joint operating agreement was opened.</p></li><li><p>Paragraph references (IAS 28 paragraphs 38–39, 41A–41C and 42; IFRS 9 paragraphs 5.7.5 and B5.7.1) come from knowledge of the IFRS texts and were not opened. The PSAK equivalents are assumed to follow the same paragraph numbering, and the former numbers for PSAK 111, 110, 105 and 221 were not checked.</p></li><li><p>The page inference assumes a reclassified investment would appear in a current line that grew. A reclassification could be offset by an unrelated fall in the same line.</p></li></ul><h2>References</h2><ol><li><p>Owner's study notes, "Inter 2 - Chapter 17 - Investment.pdf" (<code>C:\Users\USER\Downloads\Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan\</code>). NOTES. Incurred-loss impairment corrected to ECL.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 228, <em>Investments in Associates and Joint Ventures</em> (IAS 28). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 109, <em>Financial Instruments</em> (IFRS 9). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 236, <em>Impairment of Assets</em> (IAS 36). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 111, <em>Joint Arrangements</em> (IFRS 11). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 110, <em>Consolidated Financial Statements</em> (IFRS 10), and PSAK 112, <em>Disclosure of Interests in Other Entities</em> (IFRS 12). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 201, <em>Presentation of Financial Statements</em> (IAS 1), and PSAK 221, <em>The Effects of Changes in Foreign Exchange Rates</em> (IAS 21). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li><li><p>PSAK 105, <em>Non-current Assets Held for Sale and Discontinued Operations</em> (IFRS 5), and PSAK 106, <em>Exploration for and Evaluation of Mineral Resources</em> (IFRS 6). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.</p></li></ol>$c$,
       content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"In brief","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The line mixes holdings under different rules. Associates (significant influence) and joint ventures (joint control of net assets) use the equity method, small equity stakes sit at fair value, and some debt sits at amortised cost. Subsidiaries never appear on the consolidated line.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"An equity-method investment falls with every dividend received, because the profit behind the dividend was booked when the investee earned it. A profitable associate that pays out generously shrinks the line.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"A fall has five possible sources (shares of losses, dividends, impairment, disposal or reclassification, and fair-value or currency changes), and only some are losses. In the constructed 2025 case, USD 29.0 million of a USD 49.0 million fall is cash received or a move to current assets.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The line fell 30.8 percent, and the page alone cannot say how much of that was a loss","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"On the page, long-term investments fell from 1,602,821 at 31 December 2023 to 1,109,172 at 31 December 2024, in thousands, a fall of 493,649 or 30.8 percent. The line's share of total assets dropped from 5.1 percent to 3.7 percent, and the page gives no notes reference for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Hulu Energi Nusantara (\"HEN\") is an upstream contractor operating production sharing contracts (PSCs) with SKK Migas, the government body that supervises upstream oil and gas. HEN is fictional and every HEN figure is constructed. It reports in US dollars under Indonesian SAK, and all HEN amounts are in USD million. At the audit committee meeting on the 2025 accounts, a member reads that long-term investments fell from USD 160.0 million at 31 December 2024 to USD 111.0 million at 31 December 2025, a fall of 30.6 percent, and asks two questions. Did HEN lose USD 49.0 million on its stakes? And should the committee accept management's USD 17.0 million write-down of HEN's LNG joint venture?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The governing claim of this essay is that a fall in long-term investments says nothing about value until it is split by mechanism. Dividends from equity-method investees and reclassifications to current assets reduce the line without any loss, while shares of profit and loss, impairments and fair-value changes record changes in value, and each follows its own rule. This is a mechanism essay. Its verdict is that USD 29.0 million of HEN's fall is cash received or a change of line, and USD 20.0 million is a net value change (USD 32.0 million of losses against USD 12.0 million of share of profit). The figure the committee must challenge is the USD 17.0 million impairment, because it rests on management's own forecast.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK numbers follow the 2024 scheme (old numbers: 228 was 15, 109 was 71, 236 was 48, 111 was 66, 110 was 65, 201 was 1, 221 was 10); IFRS equivalents are in the references.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The line holds whatever the investor influences without controlling, and subsidiaries never sit on it","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Which rule measures a holding depends on the investor's power over the investee, and the ownership percentage only guides that judgment. HEN's line held five items:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Holding","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Stake","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Relationship","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Measurement","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"31 Dec 2024, USD million","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Pipa Gas Selat, gas pipeline","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"30%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Associate","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Equity method","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"62.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Kilang LNG Timur, LNG plant","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"50%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Joint venture","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Equity method","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"48.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Cakra Eksplorasi, holds an exploration PSC","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"25%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Associate","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Equity method","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"6.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Jasa Sumur Tbk (listed), oilfield services","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"4%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Equity instrument","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Fair value through other comprehensive income, elected","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"30.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Republic of Indonesia USD bond, due 30 June 2026","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"n/a","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Debt instrument","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Amortised cost","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"14.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Total","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"160.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Below 20 percent an equity investor is presumed to lack significant influence, and PSAK 109 measures the shares at fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL), unless the investor elects at initial recognition, irrevocably and for shares not held for trading, to send fair-value changes to other comprehensive income (FVOCI). From 20 to 50 percent the investor is presumed to have significant influence, the power to take part in the investee's financial and operating decisions without controlling them, and PSAK 228 requires the equity method. Both presumptions can be rebutted. A joint venture, where the parties share control by unanimous consent and have rights to the net assets, also uses the equity method. Control under PSAK 110, usually but not always gained through a majority of the votes, replaces the investment with the subsidiary's assets and liabilities line by line. The study notes show a subsidiary as a long-term investment, which holds only in the parent's separate statements.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Debt is sorted by two tests in PSAK 109, the business model (hold to collect, collect and sell, or neither) and whether the contractual cash flows are only principal and interest on the principal. HEN holds its 5 percent bond, bought at par, to maturity, so it sits at amortised cost. A bond held to collect and sell would sit at FVOCI and recycle on sale, meaning the gains parked in OCI are moved into profit when the bond is sold.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The notes impair amortised-cost debt only after a loss event; PSAK 109 replaced that incurred-loss approach with expected credit losses (ECL), booked from the day of purchase. Stage 1 carries twelve months of expected loss. Stage 2 carries lifetime loss once credit risk has risen significantly. Stage 3, once the borrower has actually defaulted or is in severe distress (credit-impaired), keeps lifetime loss but computes interest income on the carrying amount net of the allowance. HEN's bond is in stage 1, where the allowance multiplies the chance of default within a year, the share lost on default, and the amount at risk:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"12-month ECL = probability of default × loss given default × exposure","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"= 0.3% × 40% × USD 14.0 million = USD 0.0168 million","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The allowance rounds to zero at one decimal, so the bond is carried at USD 14.0 million. It also marks the line's current boundary. At 31 December 2025 it falls due within twelve months, so PSAK 201 moves USD 14.0 million to current assets with no change in value. An equity-method investment stays non-current unless it is held for sale under PSAK 105 (was 58).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Under the equity method a dividend is cash leaving the investment, because the profit behind it was booked when the investee earned it","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The equity method treats the stake as a claim on the investee's net assets, booking income when they grow and cash, but no income, when they are paid out. HEN bought 30 percent of PT Pipa Gas Selat on 1 January 2023 for USD 56.0 million, exactly 30 percent of its fair net assets, so no goodwill sits inside the investment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"USD million","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2023","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2024","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2025","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Opening carrying amount","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"56.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"59.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"62.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Pipeline net profit, 100%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"30.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"36.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"40.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Add HEN's 30% share of profit","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"9.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"10.8","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"12.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Pipeline dividends paid, 100%","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"20.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"26.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"50.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Less HEN's 30% of dividends","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"6.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"7.8","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"15.0","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Closing carrying amount","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"59.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"62.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"59.0","type":"text"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Investment in associate 12.0 / Cr Share of profit of associates 12.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Cash 15.0 / Cr Investment in associate 15.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The pipeline's USD 40.0 million profit raised HEN's claim by USD 12.0 million, recognised as income. Its USD 50.0 million dividend cut the claim by USD 15.0 million and raised HEN's cash by the same amount. Booking the 15.0 as income too would report 27.0 of income on 12.0 of earnings and leave 74.0 on the line while 15.0 sat in the bank. The pipeline used cash released by refinancing its own debt to pay out 125 percent of its 2025 profit, so HEN's most profitable associate shrank the line by USD 3.0 million in its best year.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"An equity-method investment is tested for impairment as one asset, so the whole write-down can later be reversed","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Kilang LNG Timur's commissioning, the testing and start-up of the plant, slipped by a year in 2025, and its buyers reopened the offtake price, the contracted price for the LNG they take. The joint venture lost USD 8.0 million in the year, of which HEN's half is USD 4.0 million:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Share of loss of joint ventures 4.0 / Cr Investment in joint venture 4.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Evidence such as a significant adverse change in the investee's market (IAS 28 paragraphs 41A–41C) triggers a test of the whole carrying amount under PSAK 236. The carrying amount is compared with the recoverable amount, the higher of value in use (the present value of the cash flows the investment is expected to produce) and fair value less costs of disposal. Management's discounted model of HEN's share of the joint venture's cash flows gives a value in use of USD 27.0 million (constructed input). A buyer has offered USD 25.0 million, non-binding, and selling would cost USD 0.5 million.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Carrying amount before the test = 48.0 − 4.0 = 44.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Fair value less costs of disposal = 25.0 − 0.5 = 24.5","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Recoverable amount = higher of 27.0 and 24.5 = 27.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Impairment loss = 44.0 − 27.0 = 17.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Impairment loss on investment in joint venture 17.0 / Cr Investment in joint venture 17.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The loss is larger than HEN's whole 12.0 share of the pipeline's profit in its best year.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 236 never reverses a goodwill impairment, so it matters that an equity-method investment is tested as one asset and no part of its loss is allocated to goodwill inside it (IAS 28 paragraph 42). HEN paid no premium for Kilang either. If the estimates behind the recoverable amount improve, for example once the plant starts up, all USD 17.0 million can be reversed, up to the carrying amount the investment would have had without the impairment.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Every USD 1.0 million added to value in use removes USD 1.0 million of loss until value in use reaches USD 44.0 million; on the downside the fair-value floor of USD 24.5 million caps the loss at USD 19.5 million.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"When the share of losses exceeds the investment, the investor stops at zero and tracks the rest off the books","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PT Cakra Eksplorasi drilled a dry exploration well in 2025, wrote off its exploration and evaluation assets under PSAK 106 (was 64), and reported a net loss after tax of USD 40.0 million (constructed). HEN's 25 percent share is larger than its investment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Share of loss = 25% × 40.0 = 10.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Loss recognised, limited to the carrying amount = 6.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Loss not recognised, tracked outside the accounts = 10.0 − 6.0 = 4.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Share of loss of associates 6.0 / Cr Investment in associate 6.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 228 stops loss recognition when the investor's interest reaches zero (IAS 28 paragraphs 38–39). The interest includes long-term interests that form part of the net investment, such as a shareholder loan with no planned repayment. Beyond them a liability arises only from a legal obligation, a constructive obligation (one created by the investor's own conduct or promises), or payments made on the associate's behalf. HEN has none of these. If Cakra earns USD 20.0 million in 2026, HEN's share is USD 5.0 million, the first USD 4.0 million offsets the unrecognised loss, and HEN books USD 1.0 million.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"A commitment to meet an associate's cash calls (the operator's requests for each partner's share of spending) may be the obligation that turns an unrecognised loss into a provision.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Below 20 percent at FVOCI, the dividend is income and the value change never reaches profit","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"HEN holds 200 million shares of PT Jasa Sumur Tbk, 4 percent of the company, to secure drilling services, and elected FVOCI when it bought them. The shares trade in rupiah. Under PSAK 221 their fair value is translated at the rate on the measurement date, and because an FVOCI share's whole fair-value change goes to OCI, the currency part goes there too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"31 Dec 2024: 200 million × IDR 2,400 = IDR 480 billion; at IDR 16,000 per USD = USD 30.0 million","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"31 Dec 2025: 200 million × IDR 2,080 = IDR 416 billion; at IDR 16,640 per USD = USD 25.0 million","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Price effect, at the opening rate = 200 million × (IDR 2,080 − IDR 2,400) / 16,000 = −USD 4.0 million","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Currency effect = IDR 416 billion / 16,640 − IDR 416 billion / 16,000 = 25.0 − 26.0 = −USD 1.0 million","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Other comprehensive income, fair value reserve 5.0 / Cr Investment in equity instruments 5.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Both effects land in the same reserve; the reader's split shows that one fifth of the fall comes from the dollar strengthening 4 percent against the rupiah, from IDR 16,000 to IDR 16,640.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Jasa Sumur also paid a dividend of IDR 80 a share, IDR 16 billion in total, received when the rate was IDR 16,000:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dr Cash 1.0 / Cr Dividend income 1.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Here the dividend is income, because HEN never booked a share of Jasa Sumur's profit; the exception is a dividend that clearly recovers part of the cost. The fair-value loss never reaches profit. FVOCI equity has no impairment test under PSAK 109, and on sale the cumulative reserve may move to retained earnings within equity but is never recycled (IFRS 9 paragraphs 5.7.5 and B5.7.1). The USD 5.0 million fall reduces HEN's total comprehensive income and leaves its profit untouched in every year.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"A participating interest in a PSC is usually a joint operation, so most of an upstream group's partnerships never reach this line","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"An upstream group's most common partnership, a participating interest in a PSC shared under a joint operating agreement, usually stays off this line. Under PSAK 111, parties to a joint operation have rights to the assets and obligations for the liabilities and recognise their own shares of each, while parties to a joint venture have rights only to the net assets and use the equity method. A contractor party to the PSC takes its share of production and bears its share of costs, the profile of a joint operation. Many operating agreements let a majority of partners decide, so no joint control exists and the arrangement falls outside PSAK 111, but each partner still recognises its own share. Either way, a participating interest held directly by HEN would appear inside oil and gas properties, receivables, payables, revenue and costs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The boundary moves with the legal vehicle. Indonesian practice ring-fences PSCs, keeping each contract's costs and taxes separate and often holding each contract in its own company, so a partner may own shares in that company instead of the participating interest. HEN's 25 percent of PT Cakra Eksplorasi is that case, an associate measured in one line although its economics resemble a 25 percent participating interest. A separate company points toward a joint venture without settling it, because the agreements decide: if they give the parties the output and make them fund the liabilities, PSAK 111 still finds a joint operation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"HEN's USD 49.0 million fall is USD 29.0 million of cash and reclassification and a USD 20.0 million net value change","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Only one row of HEN's 2025 roll-forward rests on HEN management's own forecast. The rest come from the investees' audited results, a quoted price, an exchange rate or a maturity date.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Mechanism","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Holding","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"USD million","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Nature","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"31 Dec 2024","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"160.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Share of profit","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Pipa Gas Selat","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"+12.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Share of loss","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Kilang LNG Timur","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−4.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Share of loss, limited to carrying amount","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Cakra Eksplorasi","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−6.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Dividends received","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Pipa Gas Selat","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−15.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Cash","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Impairment","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Kilang LNG Timur","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−17.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Fair value, price","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Jasa Sumur","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−4.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Fair value, currency","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Jasa Sumur","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−1.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Reclassified to current assets","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Bond","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"−14.0","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Line","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"31 Dec 2025","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"111.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"align":null,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Change = 111.0 − 160.0 = −49.0, or −30.6%","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Cash received and change of line = 15.0 + 14.0 = 29.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Losses = 4.0 + 6.0 + 17.0 + 4.0 + 1.0 = 32.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Net value change recognised in profit and OCI = 32.0 − 12.0 = 20.0","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Profit for 2025 carries 12.0 − 4.0 − 6.0 − 17.0 = −15.0 of the net value change and OCI −5.0. Pairing the pipeline's profit with value and its dividend with cash is a choice of presentation; netting the two instead would show only 3.0 of dividends in excess of earnings.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"HEN did not lose USD 49.0 million. It recognised USD 32.0 million of losses against USD 12.0 million of share of profit, and USD 17.0 million of those losses rests on a forecast. The committee should not accept the impairment until management has tested the three inputs that drive value in use (the commissioning date, the renegotiated offtake price and the discount rate), and should require disclosure under PSAK 112 of the USD 4.0 million unrecognised loss in Cakra with any funding commitment behind it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"A reader of the reported page can triangulate from the share of results and impairment lines in the income statement, dividends received in the cash flow statement, and fair-value movements in OCI. No current line that could hold a reclassified investment grew materially (other current assets rose 1,997 thousand), and the page has no short-term investment or held-for-sale line, so it shows no sign of a large reclassification.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Least-confident assertions","type":"text"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The joint operation reading of a PSC participating interest is the usual pattern, not a verified rule. Whether joint control exists depends on the operating agreement's voting terms, and where a PSC is held through a ring-fenced company the classification under PSAK 111 turns on that company's agreements. No actual PSC or joint operating agreement was opened.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Paragraph references (IAS 28 paragraphs 38–39, 41A–41C and 42; IFRS 9 paragraphs 5.7.5 and B5.7.1) come from knowledge of the IFRS texts and were not opened. The PSAK equivalents are assumed to follow the same paragraph numbering, and the former numbers for PSAK 111, 110, 105 and 221 were not checked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"The page inference assumes a reclassified investment would appear in a current line that grew. A reclassification could be offset by an unrelated fall in the same line.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"References","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"type":null,"start":1},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Owner's study notes, \"Inter 2 - Chapter 17 - Investment.pdf\" (","type":"text"},{"text":"C:\\Users\\USER\\Downloads\\Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan\\","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"text":"). NOTES. Incurred-loss impairment corrected to ECL.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 228, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Investments in Associates and Joint Ventures","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IAS 28). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 109, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Financial Instruments","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 9). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 236, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Impairment of Assets","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IAS 36). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 111, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Joint Arrangements","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 11). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 110, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Consolidated Financial Statements","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 10), and PSAK 112, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Disclosure of Interests in Other Entities","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 12). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 201, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Presentation of Financial Statements","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IAS 1), and PSAK 221, ","type":"text"},{"text":"The Effects of Changes in Foreign Exchange Rates","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IAS 21). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"PSAK 105, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Non-current Assets Held for Sale and Discontinued Operations","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 5), and PSAK 106, ","type":"text"},{"text":"Exploration for and Evaluation of Mineral Resources","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (IFRS 6). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb,
       presentation = $p${"deck":"How the equity method, impairment and FVOCI each move the line, and how a reader separates cash received from value lost","genre":null,"author_bio":null,"references":[],"hero_caption":null,"key_takeaways":["The line mixes holdings under different rules. Associates (significant influence) and joint ventures (joint control of net assets) use the equity method, small equity stakes sit at fair value, and some debt sits at amortised cost. Subsidiaries never appear on the consolidated line.","An equity-method investment falls with every dividend received, because the profit behind the dividend was booked when the investee earned it. A profitable associate that pays out generously shrinks the line.","A fall has five possible sources (shares of losses, dividends, impairment, disposal or reclassification, and fair-value or currency changes), and only some are losses. In the constructed 2025 case, USD 29.0 million of a USD 49.0 million fall is cash received or a move to current assets."],"revision_note":null}$p$::jsonb,
       updated_at = now()
 WHERE id = '52d4154e-3e35-4862-819d-1ff6dee62606';
